Endorse only the relays the media fanout connected to, and close the fanout when the call ends.

Origin: fazer-ai/whatsapp-connector, on top of 0002 (upstream PR #26) and 0004.

Why:

- onRelayLatency endorses every relay in the offer. The caller probes twice, once
  while ringing and again about a second after accept (seen in the spike logs of
  fazer-ai/whatsapp-connector#235: fanout established at 13:01:13, second probe
  round at 13:01:14), and the second round elects the relay its media moves to. A
  relay that failed to connect, or that 0004 left out for missing its 2 s grace,
  was still endorsed then, and electing it silences inbound audio while another
  relay is connected. connectAndAllocateAll now reports each relay as it connects,
  runMedia records it, and once the first one has, onRelayLatency answers only for
  the connected ones. Recording as they connect, rather than when collection ends,
  matters because the post-accept probes can land inside the grace. Before any
  relay connects it still answers for the offered ones, all there is to go on.
- The fanout's Recv waits for a packet or for the fanout to close, not for the
  call's context, so a relay that went quiet with its transport still open held
  the media goroutine, the relay readers and the sockets past hangup. runMedia now
  closes the fanout when its context ends.

Found in the review of fazer-ai/whatsapp-connector#387 (rounds 1, 7, 8 and 9);
tracked as fazer-ai/whatsapp-connector#388.

